{
  "rule": "What a file name makes of an attachment: the stored extension is the last component's lower-case extension (1 to 10 letters or digits, after a non-empty stem), otherwise none; a video or audio extension gives that kind, everything else is a file. Rust decides `image` by the file's header; the mock can only see the name, so every image case here names a real image format (`imageFormat`), and a file that is named like an image but is not one is deliberately not pinned. Only the MIME type of an image is pinned: the mock gives other files a generic one.",
  "rust": "kinige_domain::attachment::{stored_ext, classify}",
  "mock": "web/src/api/mockAttachments.ts mockAttachment",
  "cases": [
    { "name": "photo.jpg", "imageFormat": "jpeg", "kind": "image", "mime": "image/jpeg" },
    { "name": "photo.JPEG", "imageFormat": "jpeg", "kind": "image", "mime": "image/jpeg" },
    { "name": "scan.png", "imageFormat": "png", "kind": "image", "mime": "image/png" },
    { "name": "loop.gif", "imageFormat": "gif", "kind": "image", "mime": "image/gif" },
    { "name": "pic.webp", "imageFormat": "webp", "kind": "image", "mime": "image/webp" },
    { "name": "clip.mp4", "kind": "video" },
